id: pm-memory-c3gv
title: Refuse stale merge receipts after intervening memory edits
description: "Follow-up on an already-resolved PR 1 thread, outside the ten currently unresolved review requests: receipt replay can overwrite acknowledged target edits or cancel a subsequently edited source."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-memory#15",identity,review-blocker
created_at: "2026-10-19T19:35:29.756Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T07:03:09.522Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Capture and validate target and source revisions before receipt replay; preserve or refuse intervening edits without clearing the pending operation; retain exactly-once retries without intervening edits; prove with synthetic real-tracker interruption tests and both unchanged release gates.
parent: pm-memory-0kwy
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T22:54:13.683Z",codex-agent,"Self-review reproduced unsafe pending merge replay. Added durable semantic revision bindings for source and destination, validate every pending receipt before planned writes, accept before/after publication states for exactly-once retry, and refuse stale, missing, archived or legacy receipt states while retaining evidence. Synthetic real-tracker regressions cover intervening native source and target edits."
  "2026-10-19T23:00:31.569Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: restore only consolidate to the starting implementation, retain revision helpers and regression tests, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"pending merge receipts\" test/review-r5.test.ts fails with the intended missing-refusal assertion. Fixed implementation preserves current source/target bodies and pending receipt bytes on refusal; unchanged before-publication and after-publication receipts remain retryable."
  "2026-10-19T23:17:06.001Z",codex-agent,"Verified at source head 8876955: both full immutable release gates passed 132/132 tests plus 2/2 packed consumers at 100% coverage. Source and target native edits, malformed and legacy receipts, missing or archived targets refuse without durable changes; before- and after-publication retries remain exactly-once. Implementation complete; left in progress for orchestrator verification, with claim released."
  "2026-10-21T18:42:46.152Z",codex-agent,"Reverified main 97727010814d (unchanged since audit): src/consolidate.ts:96-101 verifies source_revision and target_before/target_after before receipt replay; test coverage includes intervening native edits. This is native memory consolidation, not Git merge receipts. Retained evidence: src/consolidate.ts, test/consolidate.test.ts."
  "2026-10-21T18:50:55.192Z",codex-agent,"Tracker-only reconciliation completed. Linked npm run changelog:check passed. Final deterministic changelog and tracker health are checked again after closure; the full release gate is reserved for CI. No implementation changed, so behavioral revert proof does not apply."
  "2026-10-22T12:02:47.727Z",codex-agent,"Review evidence correction for PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6vDHmD: current main 68a7321c8e11d5f419b7b4653d028b0ccbdbc5df retains the pending merge receipt regression in test/review-r5.test.ts:93-127. It checks intervening source/target edits, malformed/legacy receipts and exactly-once recovery against src/consolidate.ts:96-101. Corrected resolution and close_reason to cite test/review-r5.test.ts instead of test/consolidate.test.ts. Earlier comments are retained as historical records; this clarification supersedes the incorrect citation. Existing closed status, closure timestamps and all other delivery evidence remain unchanged. Implementation and test files are identical to current main; this tracker-only correction is verified by the evidence itself, without a source-code revert."
  "2026-10-30T15:54:38.582Z",codex-agent,"Reopened after a real non-git tracker reproduction of a remaining identity-class blocker. A receipt captured from an actual successful consolidation is placed as a pending intent; an independent native edit changes the survivor to Native C and then restores its prior body while Date is fixed. The complete SDK content hash returns to its original value, but immutable history grows by two. Current consolidate replay accepts the old semantic-plus-time digest, overwrites the restored native body with the frozen merged payload, and cancels the source. This is a package receipt protocol gap, not a claim that the SDK lacks an API. test/merge-revision-blocker.test.ts retains the failing regression. Fix needs a versioned receipt with immutable source/target generations, durable publication evidence, and an explicit legacy read/evaluate/export compatibility corpus; no existing history may be rewritten. PR #15 remains blocked, and no code from this round is pushed."
  "2026-10-30T16:23:55.876Z",codex-agent,"Final pinned pm run retains the failing regression: 0/1 passed, source_status=canceled, replay_error=false. The old merged body replaces the restored native body even though the complete SDK document hash returned to its saved value and native history advanced by two. PR #15 now contains the verified split plan. Keep this regression failing until versioned recovery binds immutable endpoint generations; do not skip it, lower thresholds, rewrite history, or treat the locally passing candidate controls as whole-class closure."
  "2026-11-02T00:08:38.129Z",pi-memory,"Fresh agent orientation for the finalization-blocker round on PR #15: merged origin/main (5a0c851) into the branch; changelog:check passes at the merged head. Confirmed the open hole at src/merge-receipt.ts:104: the finish step clears the receipt guarding only the source proof, so a target edit at that finalization hook is undetected. Plan: extend the native pre-write guard so every receipt step (intent, publish, cancel, finish) rechecks every item it certifies against immutable SDK history inside the same admission hook, with regressions injected at each finalization hook through the real host policy path."
  "2026-11-02T00:16:42.866Z",pi-memory,"Finalization blocker fixed. commitNativeFields now accepts a certification map rechecked inside the same SDK pre-write admission hook and before dispatch: src/native-revision.ts (guard + pre-check), src/merge-receipt.ts writeStep passes it for every receipt step (intent certifies the prepared target, publish certifies the source intent, cancel and finish certify the published target). A target ABA restore at any finalization hook now refuses with a typed conflict and keeps the receipt. Revert proof: removing only the certification maps makes the three new hook-injection regressions fail (verified locally: finish/cancel/publish resume tests fail 3/3 on the reverted implementation, pass with the fix). Also validated changed_at canonical-UTC validation, and merge-history ABA suites still pass (28/28 across merge/native suites)."
  "2026-11-02T04:24:34.602Z",pi-memory,"Continuation round: verified the previous agent's merge of origin/main (kept main version fields) and its finalization fix on the current head. Independently reproduced the revert proof in a disposable source copy: removing only the certified() recheck inside the SDK pre-write guard makes the three hook-injection regressions fail 0/3 (finish, cancel, publish); the fixed tree passes 6/6 in test/merge-receipt.test.ts. The pending ABA regression test/merge-revision-blocker.test.ts now passes on the fixed tree (1/1): recover binds the immutable history prefix, so a restored native body with advanced history refuses replay instead of overwriting. changed_at receipts require canonical UTC. Committed with the tracker evidence."
  "2026-11-02T04:42:54.592Z",pi-memory,"Superseding correction for thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc6yXN2w (P2): the 2026-10-30 reopening comments describe the replay mechanism using the pre-split src/consolidate.ts digest vocabulary (semantic-plus-time digest, source_revision). Receipt replay no longer lives in consolidate.ts; the implemented protocol is src/merge-receipt.ts, where version-2 receipts bind immutable NativeProof history (hash, history hash, length) for both endpoints, a canonical UTC changed_at and the target_after payload hash, and every step rechecks every certified endpoint inside the same SDK admission hook (commitNativeFields certification maps). The earlier comments are retained as historical records; this correction states the current mechanism. The failing regression from that round, test/merge-revision-blocker.test.ts, now passes 1/1 on the fixed tree."
  "2026-11-02T06:55:01.721Z",codex-sol,"Continuation audit closes the finalization class at intent, publish, cancel and finish: each writes one endpoint while rechecking both immutable SDK proofs in the same admission hook. Removing only the additional-item hook check fails all 8 ordinary-edit/ABA controls, 2 per hook. Removing the no-op read-back certification fails 4/4 default/host edit/ABA controls. New intents are durable before target mutation; body and provenance link publish together. Unique source rationale remains in the source and pending receipt on refusal. Canonical UTC validation rejects rollover dates; earlier prepared version-2 receipts remain supported, and native author precedence is preserved. The current focused gate is continuing after a transient interruption; no full release certification is claimed."
  "2026-11-02T07:03:09.439Z",codex-sol,"Verified critical step: pm test pm-memory-c3gv --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 passed 28/28 tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips. Coverage-source bytes are frozen for the continuing focused run. Independent disposable mutations fail at each admission hook (8/8), on no-op certification (4/4), proofless document replacement (1/1) and document ABA (6/6). The two earlier linked-run attempts were an outdated fixture expectation and the runner default timeout, respectively; neither is treated as a pass. Corrected the expected preserved rationale and stored a 600-second harness timeout. No test budget, assertion or property timeout was reduced."
